===========================================================
# QUESTION : DATABASE KYA HAI AUR USKI ZAROORAT KYUN HAI?
===========================================================

- Database ek aisa system hai jo application ke data ko persistent storage (HDD/SSD)
  par store karta hai.

- Application data ko persistent storage me store karna zaroori hai — kyunki RAM volatile hoti hai. Agar saara data 
  server (jispe application deployed hai) ki RAM me hi store karein, to server restart ya crash hote hi wo data lost ho jayega.

- DB Operations do type ke hote hain:
  1. Read Operations  → Data fetch karna   → SELECT
  2. Write Operations → Data change karna  → INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QUESTION: AGAR DATA FILES MEIN STORE KAR SAKTE HAIN, TO DATABASE KI ZAROORAT KYUN PADTI HAI?
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Database ka kaam sirf data store karna nahi hai — ye data ko efficiently manage karne ke liye various capabilities provide karta hai:

- Efficient data searching/querying
- Efficient data insertion, updation aur deletion
- Concurrency control — multiple requests same data ko access karein to data consistency maintained rahe (Database transactions ke through achieve kiya jata hai)
- Data relationships manage karna — different entities jaise User, Wallet, Payment, Order ke beech relationships maintain karna

Simple applications ke liye files use kar sakte hain. Lekin jaise-jaise data aur concurrent users grow karte hain, efficient querying, updates, concurrency control, aur consistency ki zaroorat padti hai
aur yahi capabilities databases provide karte hain, jo unhe plain files se zyada suitable banati hain.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QUESTION: HIGH TRAFFIC ENVIRONMENT ME EK SINGLE DATABASE BOTTLENECK KYUN BAN JAATA HAI?
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Small applications ke liye ek single database sufficient hota hai —
saare reads aur writes isi database par jaate hain.

Problem tab start hoti hai jab traffic aur data grow karta hai.


1. DATABASE CPU BOTTLENECK
-----------------------------

Database query process karne ke liye CPU computation karta hai. Jaise:

- Data locate karna — required row kis DB page me hai, wo page RAM (Buffer Pool) me hai ya nahi — ye determine karna
- Index check karna — query jis column pe row dhoondh rahi hai, us pe index hai ya nahi — agar hai to wo index page RAM me hai ya nahi
- Filter, Sorting, Aggregation, Joins — WHERE, ORDER BY, SUM(amount) , JOIN — multiple rows par calculations

Same frequently requested data ke liye database query baar-baar execute hone par database CPU resources 
repeatedly consume / waste hote hain.



2. RAM / DISK BOTTLENECK
--------------------------

- Database server pe RAM aur Disk (SSD/HDD) limited hoti hai.

- Database data ko Disk (SSD/HDD) pe store karta hai, lekin Disk RAM se significantly slower hai. 
  Isliye frequently accessed data/index pages ko RAM ke Buffer Pool me cache karta hai, taaki
  har query ke liye disk se read na karna pade.

- Agar RAM ya Disk insufficient ho jayein → query latency badh jaati hai → application slow.

 ## NOTE:
 ---------
 Data/Index Pages, Buffer Pool, data access mechanism — neeche discuss kiya gaya hai. Yahan sirf cost pe focus.



3. DATABASE CONNECTIONS CAN BECOME A BOTTLENECK
--------------------------------------------------

Suppose application me maximum DB connections = 100 configured hai.
Agar 100 connections already busy hain, to 101st request ko connection pool me available connection ka wait karna padega
aur agar configured timeout ke andar DB connection connection pool me available nahi hua, to connection timeout ho jayega.



4. TOO MANY READS / WRITES
-----------------------------

- Jab application par reads ya writes bahut zyada aane lagte hain, to single database ke resources heavily consume hote hain — jisse query latency increase hoti hai aur application slow ho jaati hai. 
  Kyunki data Disk se/par read/write hota hai (jo relatively slow hai), aur writes me additionally transaction handling jaisi operations bhi perform hoti hain — jiska apna overhead hai.

- Indexes se reads fast kar sakte hain, but trade-off hai:
  a) Indexes khud database me disk space lete hain
  b) Har write operation pe index bhi update hota hai — jisse write slow ho jata hai (index ka write pe impact aane wale section me detail me padhenge)

- Dono cases me database ko scale karna padta hai:
  a) Reads scale karne ke liye → Caching aur Read Replicas use karenge
  b) Writes scale karne ke liye → Sharding use karenge

  Ye details aane wale sections me padhenge.



5. DATA SIZE GROWTH REQUIRES MORE BACKUP STORAGE
--------------------------------------------------

Users badhne se database ka data continuously grow karta hai. Data bada hoga to backup bhi bada hoga — isliye zyada disk space (backup storage ke liye)
aur zyada CPU processing (backup create karne ke liye) chahiye.



==============================================
# QUESTION : DATABASE KO SCALE KAISE KAREIN ?
==============================================

Database capacity increase karne ke 2 broad approaches hain:

---------------------
1. VERTICAL SCALING
---------------------

Existing database server ko zyada powerful banana — jaise CPU 8 → 32 cores, RAM 32 → 128 GB, Disk 500 GB → 2 TB.

- BENIFIT : Application architecture me changes nahi karne padte — same code, bas powerful hardware.

- LIMITATIONS: 
   1. Cost — more powerful hardware generally more expensive hota hai
   2. Single Point of Failure — resources badhane ke baad bhi DB single node hi rehta hai. Agar wo down hua, to application ka DB access fail ho jayega.

- Vertical scaling server ki capacity increase karta hai, but High Availability solve nahi karta.


------------------------
2. HORIZONTAL SCALING
------------------------

- Existing server ke hardware ko upgrade karke powerful banane ke bajaye, multiple database nodes use karte hain — jisse:
   a) Capacity increase hoti hai (load multiple nodes me distribute hota hai — no hardware limit)
   b) Availability improve hoti hai (ek node down ho to baaki nodes traffic sambhaal lete hain — no single point of failure)

- Horizontal Scaling ke common approaches:

   DATABASE SCALING  
   │
   ├── 1. READ-INTENSIVE APPLICATION KO KAISE SCALE KAREIN?
   │       │
   │       └── READ REPLICAS
   │
   ├── 2. DATABASE PARTITIONING
   │       │
   │       ├── Vertical Partitioning
   │       │
   │       └── Horizontal Partitioning
   │
   └── 3. WRITE-INTENSIVE APPLICATION KO KAISE SCALE KAREIN?
           │
           └── SHARDING (DISTRIBUTED HORIZONTAL PARTITIONING)




