# QUESTION : READ INTENSIVE APPLICATION KO KAISE SCALE KAREIN?   - READ REPLICAS
===================================================================================

- Maan lo ek application hai jo high traffic receive kar rahi hai — 90% reads aur 10% writes (jaise e-commerce me product views zyada, product updates kam).

-----------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION: KYA CACHE SE READ LOAD SOLVE HOTI HAI?
-----------------------------------------------------

Frequently accessed data Redis me cache karke repeated DB reads reduce kar sakte hain. But caching har read workload ko completely solve nahi karti.

a) Agar requests mostly unique data ke liye hain, to cache misses zyada honge — aur DB par still significant read traffic rahega.
b) Agar data frequently change ho raha hai, to cache invalidation ka overhead hota hai. Pehle Redis (distributed cache) ko invalidate karna padta hai,
   aur multiple instances ke local caches ko invalidate karna padta hai — jo ki aur bhi difficult hai, kyunki local caches independent hote hain, unhe
   synchronized way me invalidate karna padta hai.

- Isliye large read-intensive applications me application aur database ke beech cache layer (distributed cache, aur if required local cache) use karte hain 
  taaki frequently accessed data cache se serve ho. Lekin agar cache ke baad bhi DB par high read load hai, to database side pe read scaling ki zarurat padti hai 
  yahan Read Replicas kaam aate hain.


------------------------------------
## QUESTION: READ REPLICA KYA HAI?
------------------------------------

Read Replica ek additional database node hota hai jo Primary DB ka data replicate karta hai. Writes Primary DB par hote hain,
aur reads Replicas serve karte hain jisse read load multiple nodes me distribute ho jaata hai aur read latency improve hoti hai. 
Primary DB source of truth hota hai — latest aur correct data wahan mana jaata hai.


---------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION: DATABASE REPLICATION KAISE HOTA HAI?
---------------------------------------------------

- Primary DB ke changes ko Replica(s) tak propagate/apply karna — replication me poora database copy nahi hota, 
  sirf naye changes jaate hain.

- Write Primary DB par hota hai. Primary DB us change ko change log me record karta hai (MySQL me Binlog). 
  Replica us log se changes read karti hai aur unhe apne DB me apply karti hai.

