#13. BACKUP AND RECOVERY
=========================

-------------------------------------
## QUESTION: BACKUP KYUN CHAHIYE? 
-------------------------------------

Backup ka purpose database ke data ko recover karna hai agar data loss due to hardware failure,
corruption, accidental deletion, ya natural disaster jaisi koi problem ho jaye.

- Data Loss: Disk crash, server dead.
- Data Corruption: Software bug, virus.
- Accidental Deletion: Galti se DROP TABLE ya DELETE bina WHERE ke.
- Disaster: Fire, flood, earthquake.


---------------------------------------
## QUESTION: BACKUP KE TYPES KYA HAIN?
---------------------------------------

1: FULL BACKUP
----------------

- Poora database ka copy ek specific point-in-time par.
- Example: Monday 10:00 AM full backup → uske baad changes hue, 
  data loss hua → restore kiya → database Monday 10:00 AM wali state mein aa gaya.
- Slow and zyada storage space on disk (agar database bada ho); 
- Restore fast (ek hi backup se).


2: INCREMENTAL BACKUP
-----------------------

- Sirf last backup ke baad ke changes copy hote hain (chahe last backup full ho ya incremental).

- Example: 

  Monday    → Full Backup (100 GB)
  Tuesday   → Incremental (5 GB changes) (Monday ke baad ke changes)
  Wednesday → Incremental (3 GB changes) (Tuesday ke baad ke changes)
  Thursday  → Incremental (4 GB changes) (Wednesday ke baad ke changes)

- Incremental mein har backup pichle par depend karta hai.Agar beech ka koi incremental backup corrupt ho gaya,
  toh uske baad wale sabhi backups restore nahi ho sakte.
- Restore: Full + saare incremental backups chahiye (Monday full + Tuesday + Wednesday + Thursday).
- Fast hota hai aur storage kam leta hai.


3: DIFFERENTIAL BACKUP
-----------------------

- Differential backup mein wo saare changes copy hote hain jo last full backup ke baad hue hain.
- Beech mein kitne bhi differential ya incremental backups ho jayein, har naya differential backup 
  last full backup se ab tak ke saare changes copy karta hai.
- Example:

  Din	   Backup Type	    Kya copy hua

  Monday  	Full	        Poora database
  Tuesday	Differential	Monday full ke baad ke saare changes (Tuesday tak ke)
  Wednesday	Differential	Monday full ke baad ke saare changes (Wednesday tak ke — Tuesday + Wednesday ke changes)
  Thursday	Differential	Monday full ke baad ke saare changes (Thursday tak ke — Tuesday + Wednesday + Thursday ke changes)
  Friday	Differential	Monday full ke baad ke saare changes (Friday tak ke — Tuesday + Wednesday + Thursday + Friday ke changes)
  Saturday	Full	        Naya full backup (Monday to Saturday) → ab differential cycle reset
  Sunday	Differential	Saturday full backup ke baad ke saare changes (Sunday tak) 

- Restore On Friday: Monday full backup + Friday differential backup chahiye. Beech ke backups ki zaroorat nahi.
- Incremental se thoda slow, but Full se fast.
- Incremental se zyada space leta hai but Full se kam.


--------------------------------------
## QUESTION: WAL / REDO LOG KYA HAI?
--------------------------------------

Jab kisi table mein row insert/update karne ki request aati hai, toh DBMS pehle us operation ki entry log mein record
karta hai — PostgreSQL mein WAL (Write-Ahead Log) aur MySQL InnoDB mein Redo Log. Uske baad DBMS locate karta hai ki row 
kis data page mein insert/update karni hai. Agar page Buffer Pool mein nahi hai, toh use disk se RAM mein load karta hai.
Phir page mein change karta hai aur page ko dirty mark kar deta hai. Baad mein dirty page disk par flush hota hai.


### QUESTION: DBMS DIRTY PAGE KO TURANT DISK PAR KYUN NAHI LIKHTA HAI ?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Disk I/O RAM se bahut slow hota hai. Ek page ke Buffer Pool (RAM) mein load hone ke baad, multiple operations / DB transactions
usi page par apne changes apply karte hain, page modify hota rehta hai aur dirty mark ho jaata hai. In sab changes ko batch mein 
disk par flush karna efficient hota hai. Har change ko individually disk par write karne se random I/O badh jaati hai, jo costly hai.

Ye batch flush generally checkpoint ke through hota hai — ek aisa point jahan DBMS saare accumulated 
dirty pages (jo us point tak dirty hue hain) ko disk par persist kar deta hai.

WAL/redo log bhi hamesha turant disk par store nahi hota — wo pehle log buffer (RAM) mein accumulate hota hai, aur jab bhi koi DB 
transaction commit hota hai, tab mandatory flush hota hai. Isse guarantee milti hai ki committed data crash ke baad bhi recover ho sakega.

Since WAL/redo log already durability guarantee kar raha hai, data page ko turant disk par likhne ki zaroorat nahi hoti.


### QUESTION: CRASH RECOVERY KAISE HOTA HAI ?
-----------------------------------------------

Agar dirty page disk par write hone se pehle system crash ho jaye, to volatile RAM ka data lost ho jata hai. Recovery ke waqt
DBMS log file padhta hai, us operation se juda data page(s) disk se RAM mein laata hai (agar pehle se nahi hai), log se committed 
changes (jinke log entries disk par already persist ho chuke hain) ko page mein apply karta hai (Redo), aur phir checkpoint ke 
through dirty pages ko disk par flush kar deta hai — is tarah database eventually consistent state mein aa jaata hai aur data recover ho jaata hai.




-------------------------------------------------------
## QUESTION: POINT-IN-TIME RECOVERY (PITR) KYA HAI?
-------------------------------------------------------

PITR (Point-in-Time Recovery) ka matlab hai database ko kisi specific past moment (date + time) ki state tak restore karna.
Iske liye last full backup restore karte hain, phir WAL/redo log ko us target time tak replay karte hain, aur wahan rok dete hain.


### EXAMPLE:
-------------

02:00 AM  → Full Backup
10:30 AM  → Galti se DELETE ho gaya

Recovery:

02:00 AM Full Backup restore karo
        ↓
02:00 AM se 10:29 AM tak WAL / Redo Logs replay karo
        ↓
10:29 AM par recovery stop karo
        ↓
Database 10:29 AM wali state mein recover ho jayega


### IMPORTANT
--------------
PITR ke liye recovery logs available hone chahiye. Agar required logs available nahi hain ya delete/lost ho gaye hain,
toh us point-in-time tak recovery possible nahi hogi.



