#16. KYA EK APPLICATION SLOW HO SAKTI HAI AGAR JVM CPU USAGE SIRF 20% HO ?
============================================================================

Haan, bilkul possible hai.

Iska ek potential reason slow database ho sakta hai.

Suppose:

    Tomcat Worker Threads   = 200
    DB Connection Pool      = 100

Ab 200 concurrent requests aayi jinko database operation required hai.

    200 Requests → 200 Tomcat worker threads allocate ho jaate hain
    Lekin DB Connection Pool me sirf 100 connections hain

    First 100 Requests → DB connection mil jaata hai, query execute hoti hai
    Baaki 100 Requests → DB connection available hone ka wait karte hain


Ab suppose database slow hai — yaani queries ko complete hone me
zyada time lag raha hai.

Toh ye 100 connections lambi der tak occupied rehte hain,
aur baaki 100 requests bas wait karti rehti hain.

Jisse application ka response time aur latency badh jaati hai,
aur end user ko application slow lagti hai.

Aur ab sawaal ye hai: database slow kyun ho raha hai?


## DATABASE SLOW KYUN HO JATA HAI ? (POSSIBLE REASONS)
--------------------------------------------------------

1. POORLY DESIGNED QUERY
--------------------------

   Query inefficient likhi gayi ho sakti hai.

   Example: Unnecessary joins, large table scan, poor query design.

   Result: Query jo normally 20 ms me honi chahiye, wo 5–10 seconds le sakti hai.



2. MISSING INDEX
------------------

Suppose kisi column par frequently read queries aati hain,
lekin us column par index nahi hai.

Example:

    SELECT * FROM orders WHERE customer_id = 101;

Maan lo customer_id ke basis par bahut saari read queries
aati hain, lekin is column par index missing hai.

Is case me database poori table scan karega, jo large tables
me bahut slow hota hai.




3. DATABASE LOCK CONTENTION
----------------------------

## EXAMPLE
------------

Agar Transaction-1 kisi row par exclusive lock le chuki hai
(write operation karne ke liye), to Transaction-2 usi row
ko access karne ke liye wait karegi — jab tak Transaction-1
apna lock release na kar de (COMMIT / ROLLBACK ke baad).

Transaction-1 ke lock release karne ke baad, Transaction-2
apni required operation ke according lock legi:

    - Write karna hai → Exclusive Lock
    - Read karna hai  → Shared Lock

Agar bahut saari transactions same row ke lock ka wait karein,
to queries slow ho jaati hain, aur DB response time badh jaata hai.


## DEFINITION
--------------

Lock Contention tab hota hai jab multiple transactions same row / table /
database ka lock acquire karne ke liye compete karti hain.

Agar ek transaction kisi lock ko lambe time tak hold kar rahi hai,
to baaki transactions us lock ke release hone tak blocked rehti hain.

Isse response time increase ho jaata hai, aur application slow ho
sakti hai — chahe CPU utilization relatively kam ho.



4. TOO MANY CONCURRENT QUERIES
--------------------------------

   Database ek limited number of queries efficiently process kar sakta hai.
   Zyada queries aane par baaki queries queue me wait karti hain.

   Sirf connection pool size badhane se ye problem solve nahi hoti —
   ulta badh sakti hai. Kyunki DB server ke CPU cores bhi limited hote hain.
   Zyada concurrent connections par DB server ko zyada context switching
   karni padti hai, jisse query execution ka time kam milta hai aur
   overall throughput degrade ho jaata hai.



5. CPU SATURATION ON DATABASE SERVER
------------------------------------

(Jab database alag server par deployed ho.)

Agar DB server ka CPU continuously high utilization par hai,
to query execution time badh jaata hai.

DB Server CPU high hone ke possible reasons:

    - Bahut zyada concurrent queries execute ho rahi hain
      possibly because ki DB Connection pool size bahut zyada badha diya gaya hai,
      jisse database server par zyada concurrent DB connections
      active hote hain, zyada context switching hoti hai,
      aur CPU utilization high ho jaati hai
    - Heavy queries (large joins, sorting, aggregation)
    - Missing indexes ki wajah se full table scans
    - Complex calculations / functions queries me
    - Poorly designed queries

Result:

    Query Execution Time increase ho jata hai.

Aur kyunki application database ke response ka wait karti hai,

Overall Application Response Time bhi increase ho jata hai.



6. MEMORY / RAM PRESSURE ON DATABASE SERVER
---------------------------------------------

Database frequently accessed data pages ko RAM me cache karta hai
(Buffer Pool me), taaki read/write operations fast ho sakein.

Agar Buffer Pool me required data page available nahi hota
(i.e. RAM pressure ki wajah se page evict ho chuka hai),
to database ko wo page disk se wapas RAM me load karna padta hai,
taaki us page par read/write operation perform kiya ja sake.

Kyunki disk (SSD/HDD) RAM ke comparison me bahut slow hota hai,
isse query execution time increase ho jaata hai.



7. DISK I/O BOTTLENECK
------------------------

Database apna data disk (SSD/HDD) par store karta hai.

Disk I/O ka matlab hai — database kitni fast disk par read/write
kar pa raha hai.

Agar disk par read/write operations bahut zyada ho jaayein,
to database slow ho sakta hai.

Common reasons high disk I/O ke:

    1. Bahut saare READ operations

       Agar required database page RAM ke Buffer Pool me available
       nahi hai, to database ko wo page disk se RAM me load karna
       padta hai. Kyunki disk RAM se bahut slow hai, overall
       query execution time badh jaata hai.

    2. Bahut saare WRITE operations

       Har write (INSERT / UPDATE / DELETE) ke liye database
       ko WAL / Redo Log disk par persist karna padta hai,
       aur modified data pages ko bhi eventually disk par flush
       karna padta hai. Zyada writes → zyada disk I/O → slow.

    3. Missing indexes on frequently accessed queries

       Index na hone par database full table scan karta hai,
       jisme bahut zyada data pages read karne padte hain.
       Isse disk I/O significantly badh jaata hai.



8. NETWORK LATENCY BETWEEN APPLICATION AND DATABASE
------------------------------------------------------

Application aur Database alag machines par ho sakte hain.

Agar network slow hai, to request aur response travel karne 
me hi extra time lag sakta hai.

Result:

Application slow feel hota hai.



9. DB CONNECTION LEAK
----------------------

Application DB connection lekar use close/release nahi karti
(jaise finally block me connection.close() missing).

Result:

    DB connection Pool me free (available) connections gradually kam hote jaate hain
         ↓
    Eventually saare DB connections borrowed state me atak jaate hain
         ↓
    DB connection Pool me koi available connection nahi bachta
         ↓
    Naye requests configured connection-timeout tak wait karte hain
         ↓
    Timeout cross hone par request FAIL ho jaati hai
    (Connection Timeout)



## INTERVIEW TIP :
------------------

Agar interviewer bole:

    "DB Connection Pool 100% busy hai."

To immediately ye conclude mat karna ki connection pool size kam hai.

Connection Pool Exhaustion aksar ek symptom hota hai.

Actual root cause investigate karna chahiye, jaise:

    - Slow Queries
    - Missing Indexes
    - Lock Contention
    - Connection Leaks
    - Network Latency

Production me pehle root cause identify kiya jata hai,
sirf connection pool size increase nahi kiya jata.
